 finally getting some international  attention  pictures of bordisov sleeping in his  bedroom with a glock nine millimeter  handgun  and bundles of 500 euro notes stuffed in  his drawer have been leaked and sent  around the world  as have recordings of his phone  conversations peppered with profanities  and plots  bodusov has tried to shrug off photos  arguing in effect  that everyone must know that the prime  minister of the most corrupt member of  the eu  has to sleep with a gun his detractors  were out to get him he said  all that was missing was a little boy  next to me but even in a country  hardened  corruption all of this has raised  questions  the focus of the ongoing anti-government  protest is borosov's links to two men  ahmed dhogan who used to run bulgaria's  ethnic turkish party  and dalian pevsky who controls most of  the newspapers  protests erupted last month after it  emerged that government security  services  had been protecting dogan's luxury black  sea compound  cutting off access to the public beach  nearby christo ivanov  a former justice minister who now heads  the anti-corruption yes party  landed a dinghy on the beach saying he  wanted to plant a bulgarian flag in the  sand  he filmed the stunt on his mobile  released it on social media and mayhem  ensued  the main question people are asking why  is borisov allowing taxpayers money to  be  used to provide security to a private  billionaire it's pretty indefensible  but bodisov has found allies in the  transnational european people's party  the biggest grouping in the european  parliament manfred weber  a group leader of the epp released a  statement in support of the bulgarian  government's  fight against corruption with protests  still going on  and bulgarian citizens chanting mafia  outside the parliament  a defiant bordesov somehow secured a 29  billion euro package from the eu  one protester held up a sign that asked  eu are you blind  the most likely answer is that the eu  sees what it wants to see  borisov positions himself as the only  leader who can keep bulgaria on a pro-eu  trajectory  and that seems to be enough for brussels  one bulgarian source who has links to  the eu  tells me borussov is seen as a conduit  into turkey  it is well known in brussels that if  merkel wants to go to erdogan  she can go through borisov he is a  political cab for hire  as long as he keeps saying yes he will  receive his golden shower of euros  the source tells me this might be a  short-term strategy  bulgarians are now asking who else is in  borosov's network  and whether it might include forces  outside parliament that are by no means  friendly to european interests  eu backed plans for a pipeline that  would cut bulgaria's reliance on russian  gas  have been repeatedly impeded by the  bulgarian state and some say russian  interests within the country  julian popov environment minister and a  former bulgarian caretaker government  said that his country offers easy  strategic pickings for moscow  southeastern europe is the cheapest way  for russia to destabilise the eu  for the past 30 years there has been a  vacuum so it's very easy for corrupt  forces to influence things  he says borisov is now under pressure to  resign  but it is far from certain that he would  do so no matter who ends up in charge  says popov the eu  must undertake a much more thorough  examination into strategic corruption  much of the money can be accounted for  on paper but the eu should be probing  who is getting the contracts  and how competent is the infrastructure  that has been delivered  they are rewarding loyalty at the  expense of the rule of law he added  krasen stanchev an economics professor  at sofia university  argues that eu cash is being channeled  to corrupt forces in bulgaria in two  ways  one is by directly distributing funds to  businesses owned by bodisoft cronies  of 200 million euros recently given to  rural guest house owners  much of it ended up being channeled to  friends and families of the government  and political elite  the other channel is national  infrastructure funding which can be made  to look entirely legitimate  a highway construction project will be  divided up into 10 to 20 kilometer  stretches  deterring international companies from  tendering this makes the road more  expensive to build stuncheoff says  it costs three times more to build a  kilometer of highway in bulgaria than in  norway  despite the terrain and price of labour  in norway  and brussels seems happy to look the  other way ivanov suspects that the eu's  tolerance of borosov as its turkey  whisperer  points to a far deeper malaise an empire  is at the point of eclipse when it  allows its border policy to be handled  by local warlords  he said recently somebody in berlin is  making a cynical calculation  a billion more or less who cares as long  as you keep buying the good favors of  borosov  and you keep him stable who cares about  some tips  along the way the interests of ordinary  bulgarians have been forgotten  they still living in a kleptocratic  state and all they  can do is ask why so little has changed  that was guerry pev and that's it from  spectator out loud this week  thanks very much for listening and  thanks to our producer max jeffrey  get 12 weeks of the spectator in print  and online  for just 12 pounds and we'll give you a  20 pound amazon gift voucher  absolutely free go to spectator dot co  dot uk  forward slash voucher
 

